1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,996
Good morning.

2
00:00:00,996 --> 00:00:01,830
Can I help you?

3
00:00:01,830 --> 00:00:01,880
Yes.

4
00:00:01,880 --> 00:00:07,383
I've just been accepted on a course at the university and I'd like to try

5
00:00:07,383 --> 00:00:10,160
and arrange accommodation in the hall of residence.

6
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:10,720
Yes, certainly.

7
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:11,560
Please sit down.

8
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:16,880
What I'll do is fill in a form with you to find out a little more about your preferences

9
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:17,720
and so forth.

10
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:18,630
Thank you.

11
00:00:18,630 --> 00:00:21,860
So first of all, can I take your name?

12
00:00:21,860 --> 00:00:23,340
It's Anu Bhatt.

13
00:00:23,340 --> 00:00:25,000
Could you spell your name please?

14
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,302
Yes.

15
00:00:26,302 --> 00:00:31,510
A-N-U…B-H-A double T.

16
00:00:31,510 --> 00:00:31,811
Thanks,

17
00:00:31,811 --> 00:00:34,220
and could I ask your date of birth?

18
00:00:34,220 --> 00:00:37,760
31st March 1972.

19
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:38,400
Thank you.

20
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:40,000
And where are you from?

21
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:40,740
India.

22
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:41,580
Oh right.

23
00:00:41,580 --> 00:00:44,100
And what will you be studying?

24
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:46,350
I'm doing a course in nursing.

25
00:00:46,350 --> 00:00:47,222
Right, thank you.

26
00:00:47,222 --> 00:00:51,000
And how long would you want to stay in hall, do you think?

27
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:56,277
Well, it'll take three years but I'd only like to stay in hall for

28
00:00:56,277 --> 00:00:56,654
two.

29
00:00:56,654 --> 00:01:00,800
I'd like to think about living outside for the third year.

30
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:01,129
Fine.

31
00:01:01,129 --> 00:01:04,090
And what did you have in mind for catering?

32
00:01:04,090 --> 00:01:08,047
Do you want to cook for yourself or have all your meals provided,

33
00:01:08,047 --> 00:01:08,960
that's full board?

34
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:11,460
Is there something in between?

35
00:01:11,460 --> 00:01:11,771
Yes.

36
00:01:11,771 --> 00:01:13,947
You can just have evening meal provided,

37
00:01:13,947 --> 00:01:15,190
which is half board.

38
00:01:15,190 --> 00:01:17,040
That's what I'd prefer.

39
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:19,550
Yes a lot of students opt for that.

40
00:01:19,550 --> 00:01:23,942
Now, with that in mind, do you have any special diet, anything we should

41
00:01:23,942 --> 00:01:24,570
know about?

42
00:01:24,570 --> 00:01:27,390
Yes, I don't take red meat.

43
00:01:27,390 --> 00:01:29,500
No red meat.

44
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:34,140
Now, thinking about the room itself, we have a number of options.

45
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:37,660
You can have a single study bedroom or you can have a shared one.

46
00:01:37,660 --> 00:01:40,180
These are both what we call simple rooms.

47
00:01:40,180 --> 00:01:46,013
The other alternative is to opt for a single bedsit which actually has more space

48
00:01:46,013 --> 00:01:47,180
and better facilities.

49
00:01:47,180 --> 00:01:50,140
There's about 20 a week difference between them.

50
00:01:50,140 --> 00:01:55,932
Well, actually my grant is quite generous and I think the bedsit sounds the

51
00:01:55,932 --> 00:01:56,760
best option.

52
00:01:56,760 --> 00:01:57,049
Lovely.

53
00:01:57,049 --> 00:02:00,810
I'll put you down for that and we'll see what availability is like.

54
00:02:00,810 --> 00:02:04,889
Now can I ask some other personal details which we like to have on

55
00:02:04,889 --> 00:02:05,180
record?

56
00:02:05,180 --> 00:02:06,450
Yes, of course.

57
00:02:06,450 --> 00:02:09,500
I wonder if you could let us know what your interests are.

58
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:13,187
This might help us get a closer match for placing you in a particular

59
00:02:13,187 --> 00:02:13,450
hall.

60
00:02:13,450 --> 00:02:14,103
Ummm.

61
00:02:14,103 --> 00:02:17,370
Well, I love the theatre.

62
00:02:17,370 --> 00:02:18,400
Right.

63
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:22,350
And I enjoy sports, particularly badmintion.

64
00:02:22,350 --> 00:02:23,202
That's worth knowing.

65
00:02:23,202 --> 00:02:27,181
Now, what we finish with on the form is really a list from you

66
00:02:27,181 --> 00:02:31,159
of what your priorities are in choosing a hall and we'll do our best

67
00:02:31,159 --> 00:02:32,580
to take these into account.

68
00:02:32,580 --> 00:02:38,584
Well, the first thing is I'd prefer a hall where there are other mature

69
00:02:38,584 --> 00:02:39,012
students.

70
00:02:39,012 --> 00:02:39,870
If possible.

71
00:02:39,870 --> 00:02:43,450
Yes, we do have halls which tend to cater for slightly older students.

72
00:02:43,450 --> 00:02:48,580
Ummm and I'd prefer to be out of town.

73
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:52,710
That's actually very good for you because we tend to have more vacancies in

74
00:02:52,710 --> 00:02:53,300
out-of-town halls.

75
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:54,550
Lucky!

76
00:02:54,550 --> 00:02:55,330
Yes.

77
00:02:55,330 --> 00:02:56,890
Anything else?

78
00:02:56,890 --> 00:03:00,138
Well, I would like somewhere with a shared area.

79
00:03:00,138 --> 00:03:01,942
A TV room for example,

80
00:03:01,942 --> 00:03:03,385
or something like that.

81
00:03:03,385 --> 00:03:05,550
It's a good way to socialise.

82
00:03:05,550 --> 00:03:06,410
It certainly is.

83
00:03:06,410 --> 00:03:07,460
That's it.

84
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:10,790
Now, we just need a contact telephone number for you.

85
00:03:10,790 --> 00:03:16,290
Sure, I'll just find it.

86
00:03:16,290 --> 00:03:19,590
It's double 67549.

87
00:03:19,590 --> 00:03:19,870
Great,

88
00:03:19,870 --> 00:03:22,950
so we'll be in contact with you as soon as possible…
